// RE-BODY main processor (Amorph FX: audio in, bodies, audio out, no MIDI).
//
// P2: Line A is complete (BODY's engines on physically modelled bodies, concept 20 sections 2-7, 12), B and C run
// the same code and are Enable Off by default. All 73 parameters and 10 telemetry endpoints keep their final ids.
// P3: the physics knobs of every line (Touch .. Reed, Width inside the bodies) are read by 50_line.cmajor at the control
// tick; this file only hands the smoothed global Width to the lines (docs/dev/06_P3_PHYSICS.md).
//
// Signal path per sample (concept 20 section 2):
//   in -> NaN guard, DC block, clamp, bypass fade                         (BODY:587-590)
//      -> per line (Listen = All in P2): onset detector, feeds, engines, grid and slots, loudness stage,
//         Level, Pan, Enable                                              (50_line.cmajor, BODY:591-856)
//      -> sum of lines -> Width -> Low Cut -> wet DC block -> shared protector + knee   (BODY:857-889)
//      -> Mix, linear as BODY on purpose                                   (BODY:890)
//   meters and telemetry every max(1, int(sr / 30)) samples               (BODY:893)
//
// Control rate: every line runs its tick every 32 samples (BODY:579), the three lines staggered by 11 samples
// so the control work of the lines does not land on one sample. Handlers only set targets (BODY:120-124).
//
// Cmajor #94 check: the three lines are `Line[3] lines`. If a compiler version rejects a struct
// array that contains arrays, replace it by three members lineA, lineB, lineC and call the same
// functions on each; nothing else depends on the array.

processor RE_BODY [[ main ]]
{
    // BEGIN ENDPOINTS (generated from plugin/spec.json)
    input stream float<2> in;
